      {
        "id": 265360,
        "name": "",
        "username": "AmeliaHealYa",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameliahealya/{size}/7327_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-04-18T04:33:23.684Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Albavar\" data-post=\"14\" data-topic=\"28258\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/45deac/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Albavar:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’m looking to add a “negative/darkness” energy type like from City of Heroes. It is anti-life and makes the target sluggish and clumsy. I had tried to make it fit with Infernal, but it really is almost the opposite. It is like the cold side of evil instead of the hot side.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chief_Lackey_Rich\" data-post=\"17\" data-topic=\"28258\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chief_Lackey_Rich:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The lack of a canon “shadow” power (either as an e/e or materials) is an odd gap, but I suspect C&amp;A weren’t the biggest Legion of Super-Heroes readers. Their loss, many a young lad grew up on Shadow Lass cheesecake. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Outside of her I can’t think of many heroes who do shadows. Villains, sure, Eclipso and the Shade spring to mind, but heroes are few and far between.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Shadow Lass, AKA “Umbra”, depending on the era.</p>\n<p>Minor Nitpick: James Robinson’s (excellent) 1990s <em>Starman</em> series and subsequent <em>The Shade</em> miniseries changed The Shade into more of an antihero type.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"18\" data-topic=\"28258\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There’s also Alan Scott’s kid, <a href=\"https://dc.fandom.com/wiki/Todd_Rice_(New_Earth)\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Obsidian</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chief_Lackey_Rich\" data-post=\"19\" data-topic=\"28258\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chief_Lackey_Rich:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And Cloak of Cloak &amp; Dagger probably qualifies.</p>\n<p>On the villain side, that Karkull guy (who I’d never heard of) that corrupted Obsidian seems to be another shadow user, and Hawkman’s old foe the Shadow Thief as well.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Cloak absolutely qualifies. He’s directly connected to the DarkForce Dimension.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"DouglasOsborn\" data-post=\"21\" data-topic=\"28258\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/douglasosborn/48/6711_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> DouglasOsborn:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I found another hero that used shadow or darkness powers: Darksheer from the PC game “Noctropolis.” It was originally published in 1994 by Electronic Arts, and I believe you can still download it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>TV Tropes is useful for finding stuff like this:<br>\n<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CastingAShadow\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Casting A Shadow</a></p>\n<p>Most darkness/shadow controllers in superhero comics draw their power from a single extraplanar source. In the DCU, it’s the Shadowlands, and in the Marvel Universe, it’s the DarkForce Dimension.<br>\nIn most <em>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</em> cosmologies, The Negative Energy Plane and The Shadowfel are similarly described and utilized.</p>\n<p>Characters who haven’t been mentioned yet include:<br>\nThe Darkness (Image Comics)<br>\nGrue (<em>Worm</em>)<br>\nThe King In Black (Marvel Comics)<br>\nKirigan (<em>Shadow &amp; Bone</em>)<br>\nClan Lasombra (<em>Vampire: The Masquerade</em>)<br>\nNightshade (DC Comics)<br>\nRaven (<em>Teen Titans</em> cartoon adaptation, not the original comics version)</p>\n<p>I played a darkness/shadow controller in my first <em>Sentinel Comics</em> campaign. I took Telekinesis so that I could create mobile force constructs out of darkness the same way that Green Lantern rings create them out of light. I took Infernal to represent attacking people with dark “anti-life, anti-light” energy in a more “direct” way, though I seriously considered using Cold for that instead. Teleportation was my travel power, jumping in and out of shadows and using a “darkness dimension” as a shortcut through space. I took Invisibility to vanish into shadows and to extend shadows to obscure myself. I couldn’t actually become a shadow, or else I would’ve taken Intangibility, and I would’ve considered Wall-Crawling. One could also justify creating ropes/chains from the shadows for Swinging. I know that I at least considered Imposing + Presence to represent intimidating people by making the darkness show them their worst fears, but I don’t remember if I actually wound up doing that or not. I know that I didn’t wind up taking Remote Viewing to represent spying on people through shadows, but I did consider that option as well.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
