        "username": "Sea-Envy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/sea-envy/{size}/1849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-04-18T22:47:20.598Z",
        "cooked": "<p><strong>Sidebar:</strong> I once created a character for a superhero RPG who was basically a mash-up of the titular characters from <em>Doctor Who</em> and <em>House, MD</em> , a cranky super-intelligent alien from a “low-gravity” world. They were physically disabled while on Earth, suffering the same mechanical penalties that Earth’s natives would suffer on “high-gravity” worlds, so they had a debilitating addiction to painkillers, and they walked with a cane that they had souped-up into a sci-fi multi-tool and arsenal, like a sonic screwdriver crossed with a <em>Star Trek</em> phaser.</p>\n<p>you might want to look for <em><strong>Witch Doctor</strong></em> a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_comic_book\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">US comic book</a> created by writer <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Brandon_Seifert&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Brandon Seifert</a> and artist <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lukas_Ketner&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Lukas Ketner</a>.<br>\nHouse as Dr. Strange = analytical diagnosis to find a good way to remove a curse and a metric ton of sarcastic world-weary cynicism</p>",
