      {
        "id": 265367,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-04-19T12:49:47.897Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This thread got me to thinking about <a href=\"https://villainyunpublished.blogspot.com/2025/04/doctor-demiurge-experiment-in-character.html\">Doctor Demiurge</a>, an experiment in fitting some seemingly far-out character concepts another player had into the game mechanics.  Fun opportunity to flex some creative and system mastery muscles for me, and the player really seemed to like it.  My commentary throughout the post might be of some help when it comes to helping a new player craft a PC that fits their personal vision.</p>\n<p>The campaign he was for also included the significantly less imaginative <a href=\"https://villainyunpublished.blogspot.com/2025/04/phade-reformed-star-smuggler.html\">Phade</a> as my PC.  FrivYeti was playing as Charlie-Foxtrot as well but I don’t have a copy of his character - although you can see everyone’s over here:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/scrpg-starjacks-annual-1-chasing-a-dead-hand.927479/\">Starjacks OOC thread</a></p>\n<p>The game met a sudden and untimely end due to GM health issues, but it was a fun time while it lasted.  AFAIK Gruagach (said GM) hasn’t been heard from since last June, hopefully he’s recovering okay.</p>",
